# Thread And Sharing Model

A Loom thread is the persisted unit of interaction history and context.

## Lifecycle states

- **Created**: new thread from `loom` or `loom private`.
- **Active**: REPL exchanges and tool calls update state.
- **Paused**: user exits REPL; thread remains resumable.
- **Resumed**: `loom resume` rehydrates state.
- **Shared**: visibility or support access updated.

## Storage model

- Local store is always present for CLI continuity.
- Synced store mirrors to server when session is not local-only.
- Search surfaces (`loom search`) query server first (when configured), then local fallback.

## Visibility model

- `organization`: org-visible thread.
- `private`: user-private but server-synced thread.
- `public`: publicly visible thread.
- `support`: support-team access flag.

## Private session exception

`loom private` produces local-only threads (`is_private=true`) that cannot be shared later.

<Callout variant="warning" title="Design implication">
	Choose normal sessions for collaborative work; choose private sessions for non-sync requirements.
</Callout>
